        "title": "Multiply both sides by denominator",
        "text": "Apply $$\\frac{a}{b}=c$$ if and only if $$a=bc$$: \\n $$\\frac{x^3-2x+1}{x^2+1}=x-1$$ iff $$x^3-2x+1=\\left(x-1\\right) \\left(x^2+1\\right)$$",
